mingw doesn't care about case, and the instructions given by the
DevTeam state you should use
mingw32-make -f makefile.gcc
from the src directory. Obviously if you fool with it long enough you
can probably get it to do anything you like; but as I've stated on a
few occasions, following the DevTeam instructions *works* if you do it
right.

* download and run mingw 3.1 setup
* download and run mingw32-Make setup
* run src\sys\win32\install.bat
* path c:\mingw\bin;c:\mingw\mingw32\bin
* cd src; mingw32-make -f makefile.gcc
* copy binary\*.* to your nethack folder (where the released exe was)



